Blackdrift: remove Firefox/Mozilla product names from translatable UI strings.

Why: a few upstream strings hard-code Mozilla, Firefox or Focus in every
locale (about_content "produced by Mozilla", the "Mozilla" settings category,
"Firefox Terms of Use", "Firefox cares about your privacy", "Search in Focus",
"Example: mozilla.org"). Overriding those keys would only change English, so
the call sites are pointed at other keys instead:
- existing translated, brand-neutral keys where one fits (menu_about,
  menu_terms_of_use);
- new non-translatable blackdrift_* keys in a new values/blackdrift_strings.xml
  otherwise, including the About attribution "Blackdrift is based on Firefox Focus
  by Mozilla. Not affiliated with or endorsed by Mozilla.", and
  blackdrift_autocomplete_add_example "Example: example.com" (upstream deleted the
  neutral preference_autocomplete_add_example key after Firefox 150).
A moved call site fails to compile instead of silently showing Mozilla.
The user agent is not touched.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

